      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): cap fields-file reads",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nBrowser CLI action commands accept `--fields-file` for form field descriptors. The previous reader loaded the whole file into memory before validating or parsing it, so a very large fields file could be fully buffered before the CLI rejected it.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds a narrow 1 MiB byte cap to the `--fields-file` path only. The reader consumes at most the cap plus one sentinel byte, rejects oversized files before JSON parsing, and leaves inline `--fields` behavior unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers get a friendly size-limit error for oversized Browser CLI fields files instead of the CLI buffering arbitrarily large input. Existing valid fields files and inline JSON fields continue to work.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent head: `a64702559964659412e7ec43a30f8e9b709c5e73`.\n\n- Real behavior proof: `node --import ./node_modules/tsx/dist/loader.mjs --input-type=module <inline proof script>` imported `readFields`, parsed a valid fields file as `{ ref: \"proof-ref\", type: \"text\", value: \"from file\" }`, rejected a 1,048,577-byte fields file with `fields file exceeds 1048576 bytes`, and confirmed the oversized file was not parsed before rejection (`oversizedParsedBeforeReject: false`).\n- Focused test: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/browser/src/cli/browser-cli-actions-input/shared.test.ts` passed 1 file / 8 tests.\n- Formatting and whitespace: `node_modules\\.bin\\oxfmt.CMD --check extensions/browser/src/cli/browser-cli-actions-input/shared.ts extensions/browser/src/cli/browser-cli-actions-input/shared.test.ts` passed; `git diff --check -- extensions/browser/src/cli/browser-cli-actions-input/shared.ts extensions/browser/src/cli/browser-cli-actions-input/shared.test.ts` passed.",
        "branch": "qingminlong/browser-fields-file-cap-v2",
